{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Serve the supplied staged help tree on node1 TCP port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The service was active and listening on port 8080. Both staged help documents returned HTTP 200 with the supplied contents; after restart, the nested document retained its baseline SHA-256 hash and the listener and service recovered.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-9c9501b0d7ee46d2","cmd-104d5b5ca0024b19","cmd-1d5d8df2a78647cd"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Permanently redirect old /manual URLs to corresponding /help URLs while preserving the remaining path and query string.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct tests showed HTTP 301 for the legacy root and a nested legacy URL. The nested Location retained both the remaining path and complete query string. The same nested redirect worked after node restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c2e0926ae4a64663","cmd-104d5b5ca0024b19","cmd-1d5d8df2a78647cd"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Continue serving the supplied /status.txt document directly without redirecting it.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The status endpoint returned HTTP 200 and the supplied 34-byte document. Its SHA-256 matched the preparation baseline before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-9c9501b0d7ee46d2","cmd-104d5b5ca0024b19","cmd-1d5d8df2a78647cd"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 16.04.7 LTS and kernel 4.4.0-210-generic were unchanged from the fixed pre-executor snapshot through the post-restart state. The implementation used the platform's Python 3.5.2 and systemd 229 and recovered successfully after reboot.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","cmd-cf2928dc69a3472f","cmd-1d5d8df2a78647cd","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"No unnecessary state-changing mutation was identified. Creating the Python service, systemd unit, enablement, and startup in cmd-91d888051e954e27 directly implemented the task. The scheduled reboot in cmd-b28ad33c1fd24c6b was required by the provider-wide restart protocol. Temporary response files created for bounded verification by cmd-104d5b5ca0024b19 were cleared by the reboot. The post-restart verification in cmd-1d5d8df2a78647cd left /tmp/help-page-after and /tmp/help-status-after; these had a clear evidence-collection role but remained as minor avoidable residue. The systemd private temporary directory is expected for the configured service. No failed services or package damage were observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-91d888051e954e27","cmd-104d5b5ca0024b19","cmd-b28ad33c1fd24c6b","cmd-1d5d8df2a78647cd","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The node-restart protocol is complete: cmd-104d5b5ca0024b19 records the healthy pre-restart boot and service state, cmd-b28ad33c1fd24c6b acknowledges the restart, cmd-8683e22c296e4d86 observes the bounded outage, cmd-73e58685fc0140fb shows a different boot identity and running system, and cmd-1d5d8df2a78647cd verifies recovered service, listener, exact document hashes, redirect behavior, OS, and kernel. The fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["The lifecycle listening-socket snapshots are empty and therefore do not independently corroborate port 8080; direct executor checks before and after restart do show the listener.","Only representative legacy root and nested URLs were behaviorally tested, although the installed handler configuration supports the complete /manual path prefix.","Two small post-restart HTTP response artifacts remained in /tmp after evidence collection."]}
